---
fmContentType: glossaryEntry
term: "Broad-spectrum"
letter: "B"
anchor: "broad-spectrum"
category: "cannabinoids"
---

A cannabis or hemp extract that contains multiple cannabinoids and terpenes but has had THC specifically removed. Broad-spectrum products attempt to capture the benefits of the entourage effect while eliminating THC — useful for people who need to avoid THC for drug testing or personal preference. Contrast with full-spectrum (contains trace THC) and isolate (pure single cannabinoid).
